 "remarks": "A rare land offering of exceptional scale and setting on New Canaan's coveted West Side. Spanning 2.65 acres, 173 Adams Lane offers the privacy, scale and presence to create a residence of timeless elegance and understated grandeur. Surrounded by distinguished estates, the property commands an enviable position within one of New Canaan's most desirable residential enclaves. A long, gracious driveway and beautiful stone wall create an impressive arrival, opening to sweeping estate grounds with beautiful, expansive views. With the former residence and pool removed, extensive site preparation and preliminary engineering work have laid the groundwork for a custom estate. Hundreds of newly planted arborvitae along the perimeter, together with evergreens and ornamental trees, enhance the property's beauty and privacy. A five-bedroom septic design has been approved. An architectural concept by Biancardi Studio illustrates one possibility for refined estate living, with over 5,800 square feet of above-grade living space, including a private guest wing above the three-car garage, connected to the main residence by an elegant glass-enclosed gallery. Expansive windows along the rear elevation frame views of the landscaped grounds, creating a graceful connection between the interiors and the outdoors. The proposed lower level, offering more than 2,700 square feet, presents an inviting vision for a private wellness retreat, with beautifully appointed spaces for relaxation, media and",
